# Product Requirements Document (PRD): Kidscover — Feature & User Story Breakdown

**Author:** Rajasekharan Gopakumar
**Document Status:** v1.3 — 59 of 64 stories built, 4 partly built, 1 not started; see the tally at the end
**Last Updated:** 21 September 2026

*Built* means written, tested and merged. PRD §8 says which of it is switched on in the live project and which is
still waiting on a migration, a deploy or an APK.

---

## Feature 1: User Authentication & Profile Management

**Description:** Secure access and personalisation for parents, school staff and Kidscover admins.

### Frontend User Stories
- **US1.1 (Parent/Admin) — Partly built:** As a user, I want to sign up and log in using my phone number (OTP), Google, Microsoft, or Email account so that I can securely access the app without remembering a new password. *Email + password is built; Google, Microsoft and OTP are not started.*
- **US1.2 (Parent/Admin) — Not started:** As a user, I want to upload a profile picture or select a stock cartoon avatar so that I can personalise my account.
- **US1.3 (Parent) — Partly built:** As a user, I want to manage my app settings (Dark Mode, Push Notifications, Biometric Login, Language) so that the app matches my device preferences. *Push notifications, fingerprint or face unlock, language and deleting my account are built; dark mode is not started.*

### Backend User Stories
- **US1.4 (Backend) — Partly built:** As a system, I need to integrate with OAuth providers (Google, Microsoft) and an SMS gateway (for OTP) to authenticate users securely and generate session tokens. *Supabase Auth with email is built, with two-step sign-in for the portal; OAuth and SMS are not started.*
- **US1.5 (Backend) — Built:** As a system, I need to securely store user profile data and let each user edit only their own name, phone, language and notification choice; roles (parent, school_admin, admin) are set by the system only.

