## Feature 2: Location-Based Dashboard & Commute Search

**Description:** Discovery by real distance and drive time rather than guesswork.

### Frontend User Stories
- **US2.1 (Parent) — Partly built:** As a parent, I want the app to use my location so that I immediately see schools near me, with the distance on each and "nearest first". *Built with GPS; the fallback to address book / last session is not started.*
- **US2.2 (Parent) — Built:** As a parent, I want dashboard tiles showing the number of schools, open admissions and schools with fees listed in my area.
- **US2.3 (Parent) — Built:** As a parent, I want to see how long the drive to each school takes at school-run time, right now, or in time for the school's own start — "leave by 7:12 to reach 8:00".
- **US2.4 (Parent) — Built:** As a parent, I want to filter by board, level, daycare, rating, distance and first-year cost so that I only see viable options.

### Backend User Stories
- **US2.5 (Backend) — Built:** As a system, I need to query the Google Routes API with the parent's rounded position and the schools' coordinates, traffic-aware, within daily limits per parent and for the whole app, storing nothing but a daily count.
- **US2.6 (Backend) — Built:** As a system, I need to aggregate fee data into a single first-year figure per school, kept up to date by a trigger, so the list can filter and sort on it.
- **US2.7 (Backend) — Built:** As a system, I need a distance function that returns each visible school's straight-line distance, so near-me lists can be filtered and sorted in the database.

