## Feature 11: The Kidscover Standard Admission Form — Built

- **US11.1 (Parent) — Built:** As a parent, I want to apply to a school with one form, agreeing in as many words to share my child's details with that school alone.
- **US11.2 (Parent) — Built:** As a parent, I want to follow what happens to my application, and to withdraw or delete it whenever I choose.
- **US11.3 (School Admin) — Built:** As a school, I want the applications sent to us, with the child's details and how to reach the family, and to move each one through our stages with a line back to them.
- **US11.4 (Backend) — Built:** As a system, I need each application delivered to a partner school's own system over https, signed with that school's secret, retried on failure, and never sent to an address inside a private network.
- **US11.5 (School Admin) — Built:** As a school, I want to see how many families went on to our own website or admissions page from Kidscover, without being told who they were.

