## Feature 13: The App in My Own Language — Built

- **US13.1 (Parent) — Built:** As a parent, I want to read Kidscover in my own language — any of the 22 languages of the Eighth Schedule, English, or eight international ones — and to choose it before I even sign in. *All 31 are translated; nothing falls back to English.*
- **US13.2 (Parent) — Built:** As a parent reading Arabic or Urdu, I want the screen laid out right to left.
- **US13.3 (Parent) — Built:** As a parent, I want my choice remembered with my account, so a new phone speaks my language too — and my notifications in that language as well.

---

## Feature 14: Security and My Own Data — Built

- **US14.1 (Parent) — Built:** As a parent, I want to unlock Kidscover with my fingerprint instead of typing my password, and for my sign-in to be locked in the phone's own keystore.
- **US14.2 (Parent) — Built:** As a parent, I want to delete my account and everything in it, after proving it is me.
- **US14.3 (Kidscover Admin) — Built:** As an admin, I want two-step sign-in for the portal, and to require it for everyone who works on families' details.
- **US14.4 (Backend) — Built:** As a system, I need every right nobody uses taken away from the database roles, so a table added tomorrow is not open by default.

